2026-02-11 02:26:19,953 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document An Example of Stochastic Modeling in Financial Services

Stochastic investment models attempt to forecast the variations of prices, returns on assets (ROA), and asset classes—such as bonds and stocks—over time. The Monte Carlo simulation is one example of a stochastic model; it can simulate how a portfolio may perform based on the probability distributions of individual stock returns.

Stochastic investment models can be either single-asset or multi-asset models, and may be used for financial planning, to optimize asset liability management (ALM) or asset allocation; they are also used for actuarial work. is relevant
